course: dictionary
lesson: 7209
title: Pheasants and the words around them
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A pheasant is a large bird with a long tail. You can often tell the male from the female by colour: «The males have bright copper, green and red feathers, while females are brown.» The word while shows a difference, so the two birds look unlike each other.
explain: Use the words around a new word as clues. «The common pheasant in British fields was brought from Asia long ago for hunting.» Fields and hunting tell you that a pheasant is a bird of the countryside that people hunt. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Lists are clues too. «The stew is made of partridges, pheasants, chickens, hares, rabbits» puts pheasants with other birds and animals that people eat, so you know what kind of thing a pheasant is. Phrases help as well: a cock pheasant is a male, and a hen pheasant is a female.
fact: A pheasant is a large bird with a long tail.
fact: Male pheasants have bright copper, green and red feathers, and females are brown.
fact: A cock pheasant is a male, and a hen pheasant is a female.
fact: In the British and Irish countryside, pheasants are common and often walk across roads.
fact: Pheasants are often hunted for food.
exercise: «The males have bright copper, green and red feathers, while females are brown.» What are the females like? | Blue with white spots | *Brown | Bright copper | Striped like a zebra
exercise: In nature lessons, pheasants often walk across roads. What is a pheasant? | A small fish that swims | A stone found in fields | *A large bird with a long tail | A kind of tree
exercise: What does «hen» tell you in «a hen pheasant»? | The bird is male | *The bird is female | The bird is a chicken from a farm | The bird is very old
test: «Some people hunt pheasants and eat them.» What does this tell you about pheasants? | *They are often hunted for food | They live only in the sea | They never move | They are kept as pets in houses
test: What is a cock pheasant? | A female pheasant | A pheasant with no tail | A baby pheasant | *A male pheasant
exam: «The mountains of Sichuan and Shaanxi hold giant pandas, golden monkeys, takins and many pheasants.» Which of these animals is a bird? | Giant pandas | *Pheasants | Golden monkeys | Takins
